  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HO-TROSA 2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam and partners are designing (as per the request of Sida Bangkok) a follow up phase of the Transboundary Rivers of South Asia (TROSA) program for the period 2023-2027. This is called TROSA 2 or (tentatively) Building Resilience Across Shared Waters (BRASWaters). The program builds on the insights and results from the current phase, findings and recommendations from the evaluations (mid-term and end of program), and discussions with current TROSA partners during the Annual Learning Forum (held between05 and 06 May 2022in Kathmandu).

The overall objective of the program is to strengthen the climate resilience of riverine communities in the transboundary Ganges-Brahmaputra-Meghna (GBM) river basins. Based on the learnings from TROSA 1 and the changed geopolitical context in theregion, it is envisioned that there won&#x2019;t be implementing activities in the Salween basin and that Myanmar will play a linking and learning role.

Key themes that the program will focus on are resilience, water quality, leadership and the three Is (Information, infrastructure and institutions).

Some of the key elements (and implementation approaches) of the next phase of the program include:
o Basin-level planning and implementation
o Building an evidence base for informed advocacy and engagement
o Co-creating context specific narratives and solutions
o Deepening engagement with local and sub-national/provincial governments and other actors
o Thematic engagement with sub-regional initiatives
o Strengthening Civil Society Organisations (CSO)-led initiatives
o Deepening private sector engagement
o Implementing a clear strategy and approach to strengthen women&#x2019;s and youth leadership
o Strong collaboration with like-minded institutions and programs

A Concept Notefor TROSA 2 was shared with the donor in June 2022 that received a positive response and an invitation to submit a full proposal.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org ref="NL-KVK-27108436" role="4" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam Novib was founded in 1956 as the Netherlands Organisation for International Assistance (Novib), and joined forces with Oxfam in 1994.  Oxfam Novib is member of the Oxfam International confederation. Working together in the confederation, the Oxfam affiliates can speak with one clear and compelling voice on issues of global concern: climate change, health and education for all, agriculture, trade, and conflicts and emergencies.  Oxfam Novib&apos;s main office is based in The Netherlands, it supports the work of a network of local offices, the implementation of global projects, fundraising, campaigning and advocacy.  Oxfam Novib&#x92;s the Hague office contributes towards this project&#x92;s implementation.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam Novib</narrative>
